  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 22 actions (src/actions.js, built in initActions from a local `actions` object, no runtime-generated entries) and 2 boolean feedbacks (src/feedbacks.js). All dropdown lists are closed lists from src/constants.js (the module mixes them into the instance with Object.assign).",
    "Protocol: Barco Pulse JSON-RPC over TCP (default port 9090 from the config; src/config.js). The action callbacks pass the dropdown ids as Pulse method names or property values, for example optics.zoom.stepforward or ui.osd.",
    "Dropdown ids that look boolean (LIST_OnOff: 'true'/'false') are strings, as are the number option values the callbacks forward as steps/values.",
    "The number options carry `regex: self.REGEX_NUMBER` in the source. REGEX_NUMBER is not defined anywhere in the module (src/constants.js, src/utils.js, index.js), so the value is undefined and has no effect; number fields also do not use a regex in Companion. Not recorded.",
    "Power: the 'Block Standby Mode' / 'Block Eco Mode' checkboxes only matter for system.poweroff. The check is an asynchronous property.get whose callback sets a local variable to null after the command was already sent (src/actions.js:34-67), so the blocking has no effect on the command that is sent.",
    "Feedbacks read the state from the projector's polled values (self.INFO.power_state / shutter_position); polling is switched on in the config (checkbox `polling`, default off), so without polling the feedbacks stay false.",
    "activateProfile passes the parsed profile name directly as the argument object of profile.activateprofile (src/actions.js:495-496).",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ~1.4.1: options do not support expressions.",
    "Variables and presets are not catalogued."
  ]
}
